摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"File claim / protection for concurrent DeepSeek Harness (DSH) sessions working the same workspace: claim/release, heartbeat stale takeover, async pending merge area (git 3-way merge). DSH Host plugin.","id":"gh:1333745051","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-file-claim","slug":"Nwflower/dsh-file-claim","topics":["3-way-merge","concurrency","coordination","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","file-claim","file-lock","file-protection","merge","parallel-sessions","plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"File claim / protection for concurrent DeepSeek Harness (DSH) sessions working the same workspace: c"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"laim/release, heartbeat stale takeover, async pending merge area (git 3-way merge). DSH Host plugin."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-file-claim"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"[](README.md) [](README.zh-CN.md)"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> **Write in parallel. Never overwrite.**\n> File claim / protection for concurrent DeepSeek Harness "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"(DSH) sessions working the same workspace."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"When several DSH sessions run in parallel against one workspace, they have no awareness of each\nothe"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"r: two sessions can overwrite the same file, a crashed session leaves stale state behind, and a\nsess"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ion that wants to edit a file another session owns can only wait or guess. `dsh-file-claim`\nturns a "},{"id":"p5s4","text":"proven coordination protocol into native DSH tools, lifecycle events, and a write guard —\nso paralle"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"l agents cooperate instead of clobbering each other."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- 🔒 **claim / release** — a session declares exclusive ownership of file paths before editing\nthem; "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"duplicates merge idempotently, directory claims cover descendants, and `'.'` claims the\nwhole worksp"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ace.\n- ❤️ **heartbeat + stale takeover + orphan self-heal** — heartbeats refresh automatically via a"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"gent\nlifecycle events; a crashed / hard-killed session's claims are **cleared immediately on the nex"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"t\nactivity** (per-process pid check) and swept by the heartbeat interval; `staleMs` expiry (2h,\nfor "},{"id":"p8s6","text":"records without a pid) and `--force` takeover remain as the slow fallback.\n- 🧩 **async pending merge"},{"id":"p8s7","text":" area** — instead of blocking, a session writes its edited content plus\nthe git HEAD base into a pen"},{"id":"p8s8","text":"ding area; when the owner releases, the entry is **auto-merged** via\na **git 3-way merge** (`current"},{"id":"p8s9","text":" × base × pending`) when conflict-free, or applied manually with\n`pending apply` when it conflicts.\n"},{"id":"p8s10","text":"- 🛡️ **write guard** — a `tools/pre-execute` guard refuses writes to files actively claimed by\nanoth"},{"id":"p8s11","text":"er session, with a hint (wait / takeover when stale / pend) and an opt-in commit guard.\n- ⚡ **zero a"},{"id":"p8s12","text":"utomation burden** — `agent/created` / `agent/status` refresh the heartbeat, and\n`agent/disposed` au"},{"id":"p8s13","text":"to-releases every claim of a departed session.\n- 📦 **pure Host plugin, zero dependencies** — no Brow"},{"id":"p8s14","text":"ser side, no build step, `node:` builtins\nonly; Windows-friendly.\n- 🧾 **audit trail** — every claim "},{"id":"p8s15","text":"/ release / takeover / pending mutation is appended as one JSON\nline, for traceability and post-cras"},{"id":"p8s16","text":"ver / pending mutation is appended as one JSON\nline, for traceability and post-crash reconciliation."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"The DSH host has no built-in cross-session file protection, and a full scan of 505\n`dsh-plugin` topi"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"c repositories found **zero** file-claim/coordination plugins. The pending merge\narea — write your e"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"dit now, merge it cleanly once the owner releases — is unique in the agent\nfile-lock category. This "},{"id":"p10s4","text":"is a gap-filler, not a duplicate."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### Compared with the category"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Checked against 11 Claude Code / Codex file-lock and coordination tools (claude-code-file-locks,\npar"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"allel-sessions, guardex, agent-orchestrator, blackboard-mcp, mclaude, ruah-orch, knot, …):"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Differentiator | dsh-file-claim | Typical alternatives |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Conflict handling | **async pending area + git 3-way merge** — write now, merge cleanly once the o"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"wner releases | wait / deny only (\"lock → write → release\") |\n| Target platform | **DSH-native** — i"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"dentity, tools, events, guard and slash commands all integrated | Claude Code / Codex hooks; none ta"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"rget DSH |\n| Platform support | zero-dependency Node, **Windows-friendly** | Bash/jq/flock solutions"},{"id":"p14s5","text":" lean macOS/Linux; guardex has no native Windows |\n| Storage | **workspace sidecars** — `<file>.dshc"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"laim` next to each protected file (the `.agentlock` idiom) | central state dir (`.coord/`, `~/.claud"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"e/…`) or worktree isolation |\n| Enforcement | cooperative tool-layer guardrail (fail-open, matching "},{"id":"p14s8","text":"the category's de-facto standard) | hook interception / declarative locks; top tools fall back to wo"},{"id":"p14s9","text":"facto standard) | hook interception / declarative locks; top tools fall back to worktree isolation |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"For development / manual verification against a local checkout:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Requires DSH with `node >= 18` and `git` on `PATH` (used only by the 3-way merge)."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Quick Start"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"1. **Claim before you write.** Editing files? Call `claim_files` first — it declares exclusive\nowner"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ship so other sessions leave them alone.\n2. **Write freely.** Your own claims never block you; write"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"s to files actively claimed by\n*another* session are denied with a hint (wait / takeover when stale "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"/ pend).\n3. **Busy file? Don't wait — pend.** Use `pending_write` to drop your edited content into t"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"he\npending area (with the git HEAD base). Once the owner calls `release_files`, the entry is\nauto-me"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"rged when conflict-free — or run `pending_apply` manually for a clean 3-way merge.\n4. **Release when"},{"id":"p21s7","text":" done.** `release_files` clears your claims, auto-merges waiting pending entries,\nand surfaces the o"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"nes that need manual attention."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Usage Examples"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"**Two sessions, one workspace.** Session A owns `README.md`; session B wants to edit it too:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"**Recover from a crashed session.** Session A dies mid-work; its claims expire after `staleMs`\n(2h d"},{"id":"p26s2","text":" a crashed session.** Session A dies mid-work; its claims expire after `staleMs`\n(2h default), then:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Eight model-facing tools (identity is the calling session — no `--as` needed):"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Tool | Purpose |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| `claim_files` | Claim file/dir paths exclusively before editing (`paths`, optional `note`, `force`"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" for stale takeover) |\n| `release_files` | Release paths (`paths`) or everything (`all`) |\n| `who_cl"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"aims` | Read-only: who claims given paths |\n| `claim_status` | Read-only: session registry, claims, "},{"id":"p31s4","text":"pending area overview, recent audit |\n| `pending_write` | Async write: put edited content (+ git HEA"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"D base) into the pending area for a file actively claimed by another session |\n| `pending_apply` | 3"},{"id":"p31s6","text":"-way merge `current × base × pending` onto disk; conflict-free auto-clears, conflicts leave markers "},{"id":"p31s7","text":"|\n| `pending_show` | Read-only: view one pending entry's meta and content |\n| `pending_drop` | Disca"},{"id":"p31s8","text":"rd one pending entry (no merge) |"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
